# Phase 18 producer facade inventory — 2026-10-14T04:22:31Z

- Pinned Java client 5.5.1 reflection inventory now records `DefaultMQProducer` (11 public constructors, 107 declared/183 callable public methods), `MQProducer` (34 declared/42 callable methods), and `MQAdmin` (8 methods). The Rust integration test pins these counts, representative inherited signatures, and the public `sendDirect`/`sendByAccumulator` signatures.
- Source review confirms `sendDirect` bypasses auto-batching; `sendByAccumulator` tries to accumulate an eligible individual message even when normal wrapper dispatch would take the non-auto-batch path. Rust's current normal send and explicit batch surfaces do not expose those choices as direct public entrypoints. This is recorded as an unresolved P18-V01 API/behavior gap; no parity claim is made.
